  "description": "KATFUJ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C76 H147 Co2 Gd5 N2 O36 P2,C1 H4 O1. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.287-4.169 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.96-113.20°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C76H147Co2Gd5N2O36P2·CH4O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ2-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Co(III), Gd(III).",
